From 6460c5d7718f3097c233c40bd7800d221fdb5587 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 08:41:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] display-channel: trace the last 64 drawables, not 8

When a streamable drawable leaves the tree without a stream,
video_stream_trace_add_drawable() records its geometry, time and frame
count in a small ring. When a later drawable of exactly the same size
and destination arrives within RED_STREAM_DETECTION_MAX_DELTA,
video_stream_trace_update() finds that entry and carries its frame
count on, so the drawable counts towards the
RED_STREAM_FRAMES_START_CONDITION frames that start a stream instead of
starting again from zero.

The ring holds eight entries. That is enough while the drawables of a
video area leave the tree one at a time, each shortly before its
successor arrives. It is not when many leave together, as they do when
the server renders a surface for an update area request or frees
drawables because it is short of them or of device memory, and each
update of the area is split into many drawables of the same shape.
qemu's non-GL display path splits updates that way: it compares the
damaged area with its mirror of the surface in 32-pixel-wide columns
and sends one copy per run of changed columns, so a 640-pixel-wide
video can arrive as up to 20 drawables per update. After such a flush
only the last eight columns keep their frame counts, and the others
start counting again.

Raise the ring to 64 entries, enough for every column of a typical
video window. Each entry is 56 bytes, so the ring grows by about 3 KiB
per display channel. video_stream_trace_update() searches it linearly,
but only for a streamable drawable that has no stream, and each
comparison is a time check and a few integer compares.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
---
 server/display-channel-private.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/display-channel-private.h b/server/display-channel-private.h
index 4e73fa8e..9d85c692 100644
--- a/server/display-channel-private.h
+++ b/server/display-channel-private.h
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 
 #include "push-visibility.h"
 
-#define TRACE_ITEMS_SHIFT 3
+#define TRACE_ITEMS_SHIFT 6
 #define NUM_TRACE_ITEMS (1 << TRACE_ITEMS_SHIFT)
 #define ITEMS_TRACE_MASK (NUM_TRACE_ITEMS - 1)
 
